.\" Manpage for qphpscanner.
.TH QPHPSCANNER 1 "2026-10-21" "qphpscanner 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
qphpscanner \- detect PHP-backed network services, collect evidence and report
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qphpscanner
[\fIoptions\fR] \fItarget\fR [\fItarget\fR ...]
.br
.B qphpscanner
\fB\-\-web\fR [\fB\-\-listen\fR \fIhost:port\fR]
.br
.B qphpscanner
\fB\-\-config\fR \fIfile.yaml\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qphpscanner
scans network ports and HTTP(S) services to determine whether they are built
on PHP, collects the supporting evidence, and produces machine output and
human-readable reports.
It is a passive fingerprinting tool: it reads banners, headers, cookies and
response bodies and reasons about them.
In
.B deep
mode it also fingerprints the PHP version and variant, enumerates extensions
and server modules, evaluates end-of-life status, and correlates known
version-based vulnerabilities.
It never attempts to exploit anything.
.PP
It also discovers and parses a published RFC 9116
.I security.txt
and includes it in all output and reports.
.PP
Only scan hosts and networks you own or are explicitly authorised to test.
.SH TARGETS
Each target may be a URL
.RB ( https://example.com/app.php ),
an IPv4 or IPv6 literal
.RB ( 203.0.113.10 ,
.BR 2001:db8::1 ),
a CIDR block
.RB ( 10.0.0.0/24 ),
a dashed range
.RB ( 192.168.1.10-20 ,
.BR 10.0.0.1-10.0.0.50 ,
.BR 2001:db8::1-2001:db8::ff ),
a wildcard
.RB ( 192.168.1.* ,
.BR 10.0.*.* ,
.BR 2001:db8::* ),
a DNS wildcard
.RB ( *.example.com ,
which enumerates subdomains via Certificate Transparency),
or a hostname.
A URL target's scheme, port and path are honoured and override the port set.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-mode " detect|deep"
Scan depth. \fBdetect\fR (default) only decides whether a service is PHP;
\fBdeep\fR additionally fingerprints version, extensions/modules and
correlates vulnerabilities.
.TP
.BI \-\-ports " spec"
Ports to check: a single port, a comma-separated list, inclusive ranges, or a
mixture (e.g. \fB80,443,8000-8100\fR). Default: a built-in common-web-port set.
.TP
.BI \-\-tls " auto|on|off"
TLS handling. \fBauto\fR (default) infers from the port and falls back to the
other scheme; \fBon\fR forces HTTPS; \fBoff\fR forces HTTP.
.TP
.BI \-\-format " text|json|xml|csv|sarif|ndjson"
Machine-readable scan output format (default \fBtext\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-out " file"
Write scan output to \fIfile\fR instead of standard output.
.TP
.BI \-\-report " text|rtf|pdf|html"
Also produce a human-readable report in the given format.
.TP
.BI \-\-report\-out " file"
Write the report to \fIfile\fR (required for \fBrtf\fR and \fBpdf\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " duration"
Per-connection timeout, e.g. \fB5s\fR or \fB500ms\fR (default \fB10s\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-concurrency " n"
Maximum concurrent service probes (default \fB50\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-follow
Follow HTTP redirects while collecting evidence (default \fBtrue\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-insecure
Do not verify TLS certificates.
.TP
.B \-\-security\-txt
Look up and parse /.well-known/security.txt (default \fBtrue\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-include\-closed
Include closed/filtered ports in the output.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose ", " \-v
Print a line per host/port as it is probed (open/closed, PHP verdict, version),
plus subdomain-enumeration steps.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet ", " \-q
Suppress progress output.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-dns\-enum
Disable subdomain enumeration for \fB*.domain\fR targets.
.TP
.B \-\-verify\-subdomains
Keep only enumerated subdomains that resolve in DNS.
.TP
.BI \-\-targets\-file " file" ", " \-iL " file"
Read targets from a file, one per line ('-' for stdin). Blank lines and
'#' comments are ignored.
.TP
.B \-\-resolve\-dns
Record forward and reverse (PTR) DNS for each host.
.TP
.B \-\-banners
Grab a short service banner from open ports that do not speak HTTP.
.TP
.BI \-\-rate " n"
Cap outbound HTTP requests to n per second across the scan.
.TP
.BI \-\-per\-host\-concurrency " n"
Limit concurrent probes against a single host.
.TP
.BI \-\-host\-concurrency " n"
Limit how many distinct hosts are scanned at once (0 = no host-level cap).
.TP
.BI \-\-jitter " duration"
Sleep a random time up to this before each service probe.
.TP
.BI \-\-retries " n"
Retry transient network failures n times with backoff.
.TP
.BI \-\-header " 'Name: value'"
Add a request header (repeatable).
.TP
.BI \-\-cookie " value"
Send a Cookie header.
.TP
.BI \-\-bearer " token"
Send Authorization: Bearer token.
.TP
.BI \-\-basic " user:pass"
HTTP Basic authentication.
.TP
.BI \-\-vhost " host"
Override the Host header (virtual-host scanning).
.TP
.BI \-\-proxy " url"
Route requests through an http(s):// or socks5:// proxy.
.TP
.BI \-\-resolve " host:port:addr"
Pin
.I host:port
to dial
.I addr
instead (curl \-\-resolve style), keeping the URL host for the Host header and
TLS SNI. Use it to reach an origin behind a CDN. Repeatable.
.TP
.BI \-\-sni " name"
Override the TLS SNI server name, independent of the Host header. A name that
does not match the presented certificate fails verification unless
.B \-\-insecure
is set.
.TP
.BI \-\-favicon\-catalog " file|url"
Load a favicon-hash → product catalogue (JSON) to attribute matched site
favicons. Repeatable.
.TP
.BI \-\-allow " pattern"
Keep only targets whose host matches \fIpattern\fR (an exact host/IP, a CIDR
block, or a \fB*.domain\fR / \fB.domain\fR suffix). Repeatable.
.TP
.BI \-\-block " pattern"
Drop targets whose host matches \fIpattern\fR (same forms as \fB\-\-allow\fR).
Repeatable; applied after the allow list.
.TP
.BI \-\-vuln\-feed " file|url"
Merge an external vulnerability feed (repeatable). The native
qphpscanner-vuln-feed schema, OSV records (single or array) and CSAF 2.0
advisories are auto-detected.
.TP
.BI \-\-fail\-on " level"
Exit with status 2 if a finding meets \fIlevel\fR: low, medium, high,
critical or eol.
.TP
.BI \-\-oA " base"
Write json/xml/csv/sarif/txt outputs and an HTML report to \fIbase\fR.*
.TP
.BI \-\-diff " file"
Compare against a prior JSON scan result and print the differences.
.TP
.BI \-\-diff\-format " text|json"
Format for \fB\-\-diff\fR output (default text).
.TP
.BI \-\-resume " file"
Checkpoint completed services to \fIfile\fR and resume from it.
.TP
.BI \-\-pcap " file"
Write a libpcap capture of every HTTP exchange to \fIfile\fR, reconstructing
each request/response as a TCP conversation for a full audit trail. The file
opens in Wireshark, tcpdump or tshark.
.TP
.BI \-\-log " file"
Write a human-readable session log to \fIfile\fR recording each request and,
per service, how every piece of evidence and each verdict was decided.
.TP
.BI \-\-web\-auth " user:pass"
Protect the web GUI with HTTP Basic authentication.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " file"
Load settings from a YAML configuration file. Explicit flags override config
values; positional targets override the config's target list.
.TP
.BI \-\-user\-agent " string"
Override the HTTP User-Agent header.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-hosts " n"
Maximum hosts a single target spec may expand to.
.TP
.B \-\-web
Run the web GUI instead of a one-shot scan.
.TP
.BI \-\-listen " host:port"
Address for the web GUI (default \fB127.0.0.1:8088\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-completion " shell"
Print a shell completion script for \fIshell\fR (bash, zsh or fish) and exit.
.SH OUTPUT
The scan output (\fB\-\-format\fR) is a machine-readable record of every probed
service in text, JSON or XML. A report (\fB\-\-report\fR) is a human-readable
write-up in text, RTF or PDF. Both may be produced in a single run.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The scan completed.
.TP
.B 1
A fatal error occurred (invalid target or port spec, unreadable config/feed, or
an I/O error).
.TP
.B 2
The scan completed but a \fB\-\-fail\-on\fR gate matched.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Is this service PHP?
.B qphpscanner example.com
.TP
Deep scan with a PDF report:
.B qphpscanner \-\-mode deep \-\-report\-out report.pdf example.com
.TP
Subnet sweep, HTTPS only, JSON to a file:
.B qphpscanner \-\-tls on \-\-format json \-\-out scan.json 10.0.0.0/28
.TP
Enumerate and scan subdomains with per-host detail:
.B qphpscanner \-\-verbose '*.example.com'
.TP
Deep scan with a full audit trail (PCAP capture and decision log):
.B qphpscanner \-\-mode deep \-\-pcap scan.pcap \-\-log scan.log example.com
.TP
Launch the web GUI:
.B qphpscanner \-\-web
.SH FILES
.TP
.I config.example.yaml
Annotated example configuration shipped with the source.
.SH SEE ALSO
Full documentation in
.IR docs/USAGE.md " and " docs/DESIGN.md .
.SH CAVEATS
Vulnerability findings are leads correlated from the detected version only, not
confirmed by exploitation; many require a specific SAPI or configuration.
Always verify against the live service before acting.
.SH AUTHORS
qphpscanner authors.
